IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- s 3: "associated person". One function per limb of s 3(1), the proof rule of s 3(2), the carve-out of s 3(3), and one function that
-- combines the limbs. Imports prelude and daydate only.
-- The limbs return MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE (the person is within the limb), JUST FALSE (the text says no), NOTHING (the text does not say).
-- The combining function takes the limbs' answers as inputs, so a caller who does not know a limb passes NOTHING and gets NOTHING, never FALSE.
--
-- Facts about the matter ("the matter to which the reference relates") are inputs: the Act uses "matter" for the thing the reference is
-- made about (for example the extent of a power to control voting power, or an interest in a corporation's shares).
--
-- How to read a function in this module.
--   Every defined term of s 2(1) is ONE function, named `s 2(1) "<term>" <the thing> is <the term>`, over the facts a person could state.
--   The result is MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--     JUST TRUE   the thing is within the term (a limb of the definition is met and no exclusion applies);
--     JUST FALSE  the TEXT says it is not: a definition that says "means" and no limb is met, or an express exclusion ("but does not include");
--     NOTHING     the text does not say: an "includes" definition (an open list) with no listed limb met.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--   Every branch that answers "no" carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "..."`; every branch that
--   answers "not covered" carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`.
--   A limb the Act hands to the Authority, the regulations or another Act ("prescribed", "specified", "as defined in the
--   Banking Act 1970") is an INPUT named for the fact ("the Authority has prescribed ..."), never a thing read from memory.
--   The definitions apply "unless the context otherwise requires" (the chapeau of s 2(1)): that qualification is
--   `s 2(1) the definitions apply unless the context otherwise requires` in sfa-definitions-rest.l4, not repeated here.

§ `s 3: associated person`

-- src:3662 | 3.—(1) Unless the context otherwise requires, any reference in this
-- src:3663 | Act to a person associated with another person is a reference to —
@ref s 3(1) (src:3662-3663)
GIVEN
    `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context of the provision you are reading otherwise require a different meaning for "a person associated with another person"?
    `the person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is the person within paragraph (a) of section 3(1): the other person is a corporation and the person is a director or secretary of it, a related corporation, or a director or secretary of a related corporation? (Answer JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the matching limb function in this module; pass NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is the person within paragraph (b) of section 3(1): the person has, or the other person proposes to enter into with the person, an agreement, arrangement, understanding or undertaking about voting power? (Answer JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the matching limb function in this module; pass NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is the person within paragraph (c) of section 3(1): the person is acting, or proposes to act, in concert with the other person in relation to the matter? (Answer JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the matching limb function in this module; pass NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is the person within paragraph (d) of section 3(1): the person is a fellow director of a corporation, or a trustee of a trust the other person benefits from, in a matter other than voting power? (Answer JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the matching limb function in this module; pass NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is the person within paragraph (e) of section 3(1): subsidiary legislation made under this Act regards the person as associated with the other person in respect of the matter? (Answer JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the matching limb function in this module; pass NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is the person within paragraph (f) of section 3(1): the person is, or the other person proposes that the person become, associated in some other way in respect of the matter? (Answer JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the matching limb function in this module; pass NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is the person within paragraph (g) of section 3(1): the other person has done or proposes to do something with a view to becoming associated with the person? (Answer JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the matching limb function in this module; pass NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the person is taken to be associated by virtue of paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) despite section 3(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 3(3) the person is taken to be associated by virtue of subsection (1)(b), (c), (e) or (f)` answer for this person? (JUST FALSE if the association rests only on the circumstances in section 3(3); NOTHING otherwise.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless the context otherwise requires"
        IF (`the person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF ((`the person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND (NOT (`the person is taken to be associated by virtue of paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) despite section 3(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a limb the caller could not answer, so the text is not applied to it
        IF (`the person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(3) A person (A) is not taken to be associated with another person by virtue of subsection (1)(b), (c), (e) or (f) by reason only of one or more of the following"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the context otherwise requires, any reference in this Act to a person associated with another person is a reference to (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... (d) ... (e) ... (f) ...; or (g) ..."

-- src:3665 | (a) where the other person is a corporation —
-- src:3667 | (i) a director or secretary of the corporation;
-- src:3669 | (ii) a related corporation; or
-- src:3671 | (iii) a director or secretary of such a related corporation;
@ref s 3(1)(a) (src:3665-3671)
GIVEN
    `the other person is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person a corporation (as section 2(1) defines "corporation")?
    `the person is a director or secretary of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director or secretary of the corporation?
    `the person is a related corporation of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a related corporation of the corporation (as section 2(1) defines "related corporation")?
    `the person is a director or secretary of a related corporation of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director or secretary of a corporation that is related to the corporation (as section 2(1) defines "related corporation")?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(a) the person is a director, secretary or related corporation of the corporation` MEANS
    IF `the other person is a corporation` AND (`the person is a director or secretary of the corporation` OR `the person is a related corporation of the corporation` OR `the person is a director or secretary of a related corporation of the corporation`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any reference in this Act to a person associated with another person is a reference to (a) where the other person is a corporation (i) a director or secretary of the corporation; (ii) a related corporation; or (iii) a director or secretary of such a related corporation"

-- src:3673 | (b) where the matter to which the reference relates is the extent
-- src:3674 | of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the
-- src:3675 | voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation, a
-- src:3676 | person with whom the other person has, or proposes to
-- src:3677 | enter into, an agreement, arrangement, understanding or
-- src:3678 | undertaking, whether formal or informal, or express or
-- src:3679 | implied —
-- src:3681 | (i) by reason of which either of those persons may
-- src:3682 | exercise, directly or indirectly, control the exercise
-- src:3687 | of, or substantially influence the exercise of, any
-- src:3688 | voting power attached to a share in the corporation;
-- src:3690 | (ii) with a view to controlling or influencing the
-- src:3691 | composition of the board of directors, or the
-- src:3692 | conduct of affairs, of the corporation; or
-- src:3694 | (iii) under which either of those persons may acquire
-- src:3695 | from the other of them shares in the corporation or
-- src:3696 | may be required to dispose of such shares in
-- src:3697 | accordance with the directions of the other of them,
-- src:3699 | (b) except that, in relation to a matter relating to shares in a
-- src:3700 | corporation, a person may be an associate of the
-- src:3701 | corporation and the corporation may be an associate of a
-- src:3702 | person;
@ref s 3(1)(b) (src:3673-3702)
GIVEN
    `the matter is the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter to which the reference relates the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation?
    `the person has, or proposes to enter into with the other person, an agreement, arrangement, understanding or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the other person have, or propose to enter into, with the person an agreement, arrangement, understanding or undertaking, whether formal or informal, or express or implied?
    `by reason of it either of them may exercise or control, or substantially influence, the voting power attached to a share in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By reason of it, may either of the two persons exercise, directly or indirectly, control the exercise of, or substantially influence the exercise of, any voting power attached to a share in the corporation?
    `it is made with a view to controlling or influencing the composition of the board of directors, or the conduct of affairs, of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made with a view to controlling or influencing the composition of the board of directors, or the conduct of affairs, of the corporation?
    `under it either of them may acquire shares in the corporation from the other, or may be required to dispose of such shares as the other directs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under it, may either of the two persons acquire from the other shares in the corporation, or be required to dispose of such shares in accordance with the other's directions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(b) the person has an agreement about voting power with the other person` MEANS
    IF `the matter is the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` AND `the person has, or proposes to enter into with the other person, an agreement, arrangement, understanding or undertaking` AND (`by reason of it either of them may exercise or control, or substantially influence, the voting power attached to a share in the corporation` OR `it is made with a view to controlling or influencing the composition of the board of directors, or the conduct of affairs, of the corporation` OR `under it either of them may acquire shares in the corporation from the other, or may be required to dispose of such shares as the other directs`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any reference in this Act to a person associated with another person is a reference to ... (b) where the matter to which the reference relates is the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation, a person with whom the other person has, or proposes to enter into, an agreement, arrangement, understanding or undertaking, whether formal or informal, or express or implied (i) ...; (ii) ...; or (iii) ..."

@ref s 3(1)(b) (the exception) (src:3699-3702)
GIVEN
    `the matter relates to shares in a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter to which the reference relates a matter relating to shares in a corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(b) a corporation may be an associate in a matter relating to shares` MEANS
    IF `the matter relates to shares in a corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to a matter relating to shares in a corporation"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii): fork line S1 in NOTES.md

-- src:3704 | (c) a person with whom the other person is acting, or proposes
-- src:3705 | to act, in concert in relation to the matter to which the
-- src:3706 | reference relates;
@ref s 3(1)(c) (src:3704-3706)
GIVEN
    `the other person is acting, or proposes to act, in concert with the person in relation to the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person acting, or proposing to act, in concert with the person in relation to the matter to which the reference relates?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(c) the person is acting in concert with the other person` MEANS
    IF `the other person is acting, or proposes to act, in concert with the person in relation to the matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any reference in this Act to a person associated with another person is a reference to ... (c) a person with whom the other person is acting, or proposes to act, in concert in relation to the matter to which the reference relates"

-- src:3743 | (2) Where, in any proceedings under this Act, it is alleged that a
-- src:3744 | person referred to in subsection (1)(d)(i) was associated with another
-- src:3745 | person at a particular time, the firstmentioned person is not
-- src:3746 | considered to be so associated in relation to a matter to which the
-- src:3747 | proceedings relate unless the person alleging the association proves
-- src:3748 | that the firstmentioned person at that time knew or ought reasonably
-- src:3749 | to have known the material particulars of that matter.
@ref s 3(2) (src:3743-3749)
GIVEN
    `it is alleged in proceedings under this Act that the person was associated with the other person as a fellow director at a particular time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it alleged, in proceedings under this Act, that the person was associated with another person at a particular time by being a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director?
    `the person alleging the association proves that the person at that time knew or ought reasonably to have known the material particulars of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person alleging the association prove that the person alleged to be associated at that time knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the material particulars of the matter to which the proceedings relate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(2) the director is considered associated with the other person in the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `it is alleged in proceedings under this Act that the person was associated with the other person as a fellow director at a particular time`
    THEN
        IF `the person alleging the association proves that the person at that time knew or ought reasonably to have known the material particulars of the matter`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) lifts its own bar once knowledge is proved and says no more; section 3(1)(d)(i) then decides
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the firstmentioned person is not considered to be so associated in relation to a matter to which the proceedings relate unless the person alleging the association proves that the firstmentioned person at that time knew or ought reasonably to have known the material particulars of that matter"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any proceedings under this Act"

-- src:3708 | (d) where the matter to which the reference relates is a matter,
-- src:3709 | other than the extent of a power to exercise, or to control
-- src:3710 | the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares
-- src:3711 | in a corporation —
-- src:3713 | (i) subject to subsection (2), a person who is a director
-- src:3714 | of a corporation of which the other person is a
-- src:3715 | director; or
-- src:3717 | (ii) a trustee of a trust in relation to which the other
-- src:3718 | person benefits or is capable of benefiting otherwise
-- src:3719 | than by reason of transactions entered into in the
-- src:3720 | ordinary course of business in connection with the
-- src:3721 | lending of money;
@ref s 3(1)(d) (src:3708-3721)
GIVEN
    `the matter is a matter other than the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter to which the reference relates a matter other than the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation?
    `the person is a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director?
    `it is alleged in proceedings under this Act that the person was associated with the other person as a fellow director at a particular time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it alleged, in proceedings under this Act, that the person was associated with another person at a particular time by being a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director?
    `the person alleging the association proves that the person at that time knew or ought reasonably to have known the material particulars of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person alleging the association prove that the person alleged to be associated at that time knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the material particulars of the matter to which the proceedings relate?
    `the person is a trustee of a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a trustee of a trust?
    `the other person benefits, or is capable of benefiting, from the trust otherwise than by reason of transactions entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the other person benefit, or is the other person capable of benefiting, from the trust otherwise than by reason of transactions entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(d) the person is a fellow director or a trustee connected with the other person` MEANS
    IF `the matter is a matter other than the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` AND ((`the person is a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director` AND (NOT (`s 3(2) the director is considered associated with the other person in the proceedings` `it is alleged in proceedings under this Act that the person was associated with the other person as a fellow director at a particular time` `the person alleging the association proves that the person at that time knew or ought reasonably to have known the material particulars of the matter` EQUALS JUST FALSE))) OR (`the person is a trustee of a trust` AND `the other person benefits, or is capable of benefiting, from the trust otherwise than by reason of transactions entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any reference in this Act to a person associated with another person is a reference to ... (d) where the matter to which the reference relates is a matter, other than the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation (i) subject to subsection (2), a person who is a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director; or (ii) a trustee of a trust in relation to which the other person benefits or is capable of benefiting otherwise than by reason of transactions entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money"

-- src:3723 | (e) a person with whom the other person is, according to any
-- src:3724 | subsidiary legislation made under this Act, to be regarded
-- src:3725 | as associated in respect of the matter to which the reference
-- src:3726 | relates;
@ref s 3(1)(e) (src:3723-3726)
GIVEN
    `subsidiary legislation made under this Act says the person is to be regarded as associated with the other person in respect of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsidiary legislation made under this Act say that the person is to be regarded as associated with the other person in respect of the matter to which the reference relates?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(e) subsidiary legislation regards the person as associated with the other person` MEANS
    IF `subsidiary legislation made under this Act says the person is to be regarded as associated with the other person in respect of the matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any reference in this Act to a person associated with another person is a reference to ... (e) a person with whom the other person is, according to any subsidiary legislation made under this Act, to be regarded as associated in respect of the matter to which the reference relates"

-- src:3728 | (f) a person with whom the other person is, or proposes to
-- src:3729 | become, associated, whether formally or informally, in any
-- src:3734 | other way in respect of the matter to which the reference
-- src:3735 | relates; or
@ref s 3(1)(f) (src:3728-3735)
GIVEN
    `the other person is, or proposes to become, associated with the person, formally or informally, in any other way in respect of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person, or does the other person propose to become, associated with the person, whether formally or informally, in any other way in respect of the matter to which the reference relates?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(f) the person is associated with the other person in another way` MEANS
    IF `the other person is, or proposes to become, associated with the person, formally or informally, in any other way in respect of the matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any reference in this Act to a person associated with another person is a reference to ... (f) a person with whom the other person is, or proposes to become, associated, whether formally or informally, in any other way in respect of the matter to which the reference relates"

-- src:3737 | (g) where the other person has entered into, or proposes to
-- src:3738 | enter into, a transaction, or has done, or proposes to do, any
-- src:3739 | other act or thing, with a view to becoming associated with
-- src:3740 | a person as referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d), (e) or
-- src:3741 | (f), that last‑mentioned person.
@ref s 3(1)(g) (src:3737-3741)
GIVEN
    `the other person has entered into, or proposes to enter into, a transaction, or has done or proposes to do any other act or thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the other person entered into, or does the other person propose to enter into, a transaction, or has the other person done, or does the other person propose to do, any other act or thing?
    `it is with a view to becoming associated with the person as referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it with a view to becoming associated with the person in a way referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f) of section 3(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(g) the other person has acted with a view to becoming associated with the person` MEANS
    IF `the other person has entered into, or proposes to enter into, a transaction, or has done or proposes to do any other act or thing` AND `it is with a view to becoming associated with the person as referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any reference in this Act to a person associated with another person is a reference to ... (g) where the other person has entered into, or proposes to enter into, a transaction, or has done, or proposes to do, any other act or thing, with a view to becoming associated with a person as referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f), that last-mentioned person"

-- src:3755 | (a) that one of those persons (B) provides advice to, or acts on
-- src:3756 | behalf of, A in the proper performance of the functions
-- src:3757 | attaching to B’s professional capacity or to B’s business
-- src:3758 | relationship with A;
@ref s 3(3)(a) (src:3755-3758)
GIVEN
    `one of the two persons (B) provides advice to, or acts on behalf of, the other (A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does one of the two persons (B) provide advice to, or act on behalf of, the other (A)?
    `B does so in the proper performance of the functions attaching to B's professional capacity or B's business relationship with A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B doing so in the proper performance of the functions attaching to B's professional capacity or to B's business relationship with A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(3)(a) the circumstance is that one of the persons provides advice to, or acts for, the other in a professional or business capacity` MEANS
    IF `one of the two persons (B) provides advice to, or acts on behalf of, the other (A)` AND `B does so in the proper performance of the functions attaching to B's professional capacity or B's business relationship with A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) that one of those persons (B) provides advice to, or acts on behalf of, A in the proper performance of the functions attaching to B's professional capacity or to B's business relationship with A"

-- src:3760 | (b) that one of those persons, a customer, gives specific
-- src:3761 | instructions to A, whose ordinary business includes dealing
-- src:3762 | in capital markets products, to acquire shares on the
-- src:3763 | customer’s behalf in the ordinary course of that business;
@ref s 3(3)(b) (src:3760-3763)
GIVEN
    `one of the two persons, a customer, gives specific instructions to the other (A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does one of the two persons, a customer, give specific instructions to the other (A)?
    `A's ordinary business includes dealing in capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A's ordinary business include dealing in capital markets products (as section 2(1) "dealing in capital markets products" has it)?
    `the instructions are to acquire shares on the customer's behalf in the ordinary course of that business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the instructions to acquire shares on the customer's behalf in the ordinary course of that business?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(3)(b) the circumstance is that a customer gives specific instructions to a dealer to acquire shares` MEANS
    IF `one of the two persons, a customer, gives specific instructions to the other (A)` AND `A's ordinary business includes dealing in capital markets products` AND `the instructions are to acquire shares on the customer's behalf in the ordinary course of that business`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) that one of those persons, a customer, gives specific instructions to A, whose ordinary business includes dealing in capital markets products, to acquire shares on the customer's behalf in the ordinary course of that business"

-- src:3765 | (c) that one of those persons has sent, or proposes to send, to A
-- src:3766 | a take‑over offer, or has made, or proposes to make, offers
-- src:3767 | under a take‑over announcement, within the meaning of
-- src:3768 | the Take‑over Code, in relation to shares held by A;
@ref s 3(3)(c) (src:3765-3768)
GIVEN
    `one of the two persons has sent, or proposes to send, the other (A) a take-over offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has one of the two persons sent, or does one propose to send, the other (A) a take-over offer (as section 2(1) "take-over offer" has it)?
    `one of the two persons has made, or proposes to make, offers under a take-over announcement within the meaning of the Take-over Code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has one of the two persons made, or does one propose to make, offers under a take-over announcement, within the meaning of the Take-over Code?
    `it is in relation to shares held by A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in relation to shares held by A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(3)(c) the circumstance is that one of the persons has sent or proposes to send the other a take-over offer` MEANS
    IF (`one of the two persons has sent, or proposes to send, the other (A) a take-over offer` OR `one of the two persons has made, or proposes to make, offers under a take-over announcement within the meaning of the Take-over Code`) AND `it is in relation to shares held by A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) that one of those persons has sent, or proposes to send, to A a take-over offer, or has made, or proposes to make, offers under a take-over announcement, within the meaning of the Take-over Code, in relation to shares held by A"

-- src:3770 | (d) that one of those persons has appointed A, otherwise than
-- src:3771 | for valuable consideration given by A or by an associate of
-- src:3772 | A, to vote as a proxy or representative at a meeting of
-- src:3773 | members, or of a class of members, of a corporation.
@ref s 3(3)(d) (src:3770-3773)
GIVEN
    `one of the two persons has appointed the other (A) to vote as a proxy or representative at a meeting of members, or of a class of members, of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has one of the two persons appointed the other (A) to vote as a proxy or representative at a meeting of members, or of a class of members, of a corporation?
    `the appointment was for valuable consideration given by A or by an associate of A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the appointment for valuable consideration given by A or by an associate of A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(3)(d) the circumstance is that one of the persons has appointed the other as proxy or representative` MEANS
    IF `one of the two persons has appointed the other (A) to vote as a proxy or representative at a meeting of members, or of a class of members, of a corporation` AND (NOT `the appointment was for valuable consideration given by A or by an associate of A`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) that one of those persons has appointed A, otherwise than for valuable consideration given by A or by an associate of A, to vote as a proxy or representative at a meeting of members, or of a class of members, of a corporation"

-- src:3751 | (3) A person (A) is not taken to be associated with another person
-- src:3752 | by virtue of subsection (1)(b), (c), (e) or (f) by reason only of one or
-- src:3753 | more of the following:
@ref s 3(3) (src:3751-3753)
GIVEN
    `the circumstance in paragraph (a) of section 3(3) is present` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 3(3)(a) answer? (JUST TRUE if the circumstance is present.)
    `the circumstance in paragraph (b) of section 3(3) is present` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 3(3)(b) answer? (JUST TRUE if the circumstance is present.)
    `the circumstance in paragraph (c) of section 3(3) is present` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 3(3)(c) answer? (JUST TRUE if the circumstance is present.)
    `the circumstance in paragraph (d) of section 3(3) is present` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 3(3)(d) answer? (JUST TRUE if the circumstance is present.)
    `the association rests on some ground other than the circumstances in paragraphs (a) to (d) of section 3(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the association through paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) of section 3(1) rest on some ground other than the circumstances in paragraphs (a) to (d) of section 3(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(3) the person is taken to be associated by virtue of subsection (1)(b), (c), (e) or (f)` MEANS
    IF ((`the circumstance in paragraph (a) of section 3(3) is present` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the circumstance in paragraph (b) of section 3(3) is present` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the circumstance in paragraph (c) of section 3(3) is present` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the circumstance in paragraph (d) of section 3(3) is present` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND (NOT `the association rests on some ground other than the circumstances in paragraphs (a) to (d) of section 3(3)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person (A) is not taken to be associated with another person by virtue of subsection (1)(b), (c), (e) or (f) by reason only of one or more of the following"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only of": an association that rests on another ground is outside subsection (3)
